# Authentication Architecture

Splash

↓

Load Tokens

↓

No Tokens?

↓

Auth Stack

Welcome → Register or Login

↓

Save Tokens

↓

Persist user in local db

↓

Home Stack

---

Tokens Exist

↓

Validate Session (`GET /users/me`)

↓

Home Stack

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  Splash[index splash gate] --> LoadTokens[Load tokens]
  LoadTokens -->|none| AuthStack[Auth Stack]
  LoadTokens -->|present| Validate["GET /users/me"]
  Validate -->|ok| HomeStack[Home Tabs]
  Validate -->|401/fail| ClearTokens[deleteTokens] --> AuthStack
  AuthStack --> Welcome
  Welcome --> Login
  Welcome --> Signup
  Login -->|saveTokens + setUser| HomeStack
  Signup -->|saveTokens + setUser| HomeStack
```

---

# Tokens lifecycle

API request
↓
Add access token
↓
Server
│
├── 200 → return response
│
└── 401
↓
Refresh token (POST /auth/refresh)
↓
New access token
↓
Store tokens (if refresh token is also in respose)
↓
Retry original requests

## Notes

- Multiple requests can expire simultaneously.
- Use single-refresh mechanism. do not refresh for every single request.
- Refresh once -> new token -> retry expired requests

